pokeheartgold-widepointers3.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies the patches in name order): MonShowData's btlMonObjData
(include/overlay_12_mon_show_data.h, a pointer) was cleared with a 32-bit store (`*((s32 *)&...->btlMonObjData) = 0`, the
lifted DS code's word store) in ov12_0225B960 (the battle's send-out task: state 0, and after the sprite data is freed). On
the host only the low half became 0: when state 0 creates no BattleMonOBJData (the battler types and battle kinds that skip it)
the high half kept the heap's old bytes, the pointer read as non-NULL and the send-out freed it: SIGSEGV in ov07_0221FE08
(overlay_07_0221FDFC.c:193). Seen in trainer battles of the hg route chain with Text speed Instant (the heap's earlier
contents differ), the legs sprout, elder and ucave-out; the game's own text pace had zeros there by chance. Now a pointer store.
Handover-ID: none (port-only)

diff --git a/src/overlay_12_battle_controller_opponent_0225AE48_0225B454_0225B960_0225B960.c b/src/overlay_12_battle_controller_opponent_0225AE48_0225B454_0225B960_0225B960.c
index 7d5d7c3..a93462c 100644
--- a/src/overlay_12_battle_controller_opponent_0225AE48_0225B454_0225B960_0225B960.c
+++ b/src/overlay_12_battle_controller_opponent_0225AE48_0225B454_0225B960_0225B960.c
@@ -62,5 +62,5 @@ void ov12_0225B960(SysTask *arg0, void *arg1) {
     case 0:
         ((MonShowData *)arg1)->delay = 0U;
-        *((s32 *)&((MonShowData *)arg1)->btlMonObjData) = 0;
+        ((MonShowData *)arg1)->btlMonObjData = NULL;
         if (BattleSystem_GetBattleType(*(BattleSystem **)arg1) & 8) {
             if (!(BattleSystem_GetBattleSpecial(*(BattleSystem **)arg1) & 0x20) && (((MonShowData *)arg1)->battlerType == 2)) {
@@ -127,5 +127,5 @@ block_22:
                 if (((MonShowData *)arg1)->btlMonObjData != NULL) {
                     ov07_0221FE08(((MonShowData *)arg1)->btlMonObjData);
-                    *((s32 *)&((MonShowData *)arg1)->btlMonObjData) = 0;
+                    ((MonShowData *)arg1)->btlMonObjData = NULL;
                 }
                 ((MonShowData *)arg1)->state = (u8)(((MonShowData *)arg1)->state + 1);
